ars_(I).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Miscellany_on_the_Life_of_St._Edmund_-_MS_M.736_fol._9v.jpg/500px-Miscellany_on_the_Life_of_St._Edmund_-_MS_M.736_fol._9v.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Miscellany_on_the_Life_of_St._Edmund_-_MS_M.736_fol._9v.jpg/500px-Miscellany_on_the_Life_of_St._Edmund_-_MS_M.736_fol._9v.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea-faring Norsemen depicted invading England. Illuminated illustration from the 12th-century Miscellany on the Life of St. Edmund (Pierpont Morgan Library)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMiscellany_on_the_Life_of_St._Edmund_-_MS_M.736_fol._9v.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Vikings-Voyages.png/500px-Vikings-Voyages.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Vikings-Voyages.png/500px-Vikings-Voyages.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Viking expeditions (blue line): depicting the immense breadth of their voyages through most of Europe, the Mediterranean Sea, Northern Africa, Asia Minor, the Arctic, and North America. Lower Normandy, depicted as a \"Viking territory in 911\", was not part of the lands granted by the king of the Franks to Rollo in 911, but Upper Normandy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVikings-Voyages.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Nicholas_Roerich%2C_Guests_from_Overseas_%28corrected_colour%29.jpg/500px-Nicholas_Roerich%2C_Guests_from_Overseas_%28corrected_colour%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Nicholas_Roerich%2C_Guests_from_Overseas_%28correct